},{"id":"I6","predictions_lines":"65-67","reading":"Harness-failure share of a cell = HARNESS_FAILED / (all rows except NOT_RUN). 'More than 20 percent' is strictly greater than 1/5. CONTRACT_VIOLATION rows are counted as non-accepted task outcomes, not excluded."},{"id":"I7","predictions_lines":"90-93","reading":"H2 SUPPORTED_FOR also needs the ordinary cells for D, A, and C to clear the harness-failure limit and the floor of 8, and ordinary D must not beat both A and C by >= 1/6. Ordinary data that cannot be judged gives INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE."},{"id":"I8","predictions_lines":"106-109","reading":"H3 'B is not materially worse than A on both latency and tokens' is read as: it is not true that A is materially better than B on both measures. If A has zero accepted runs, A's economics is undefined, so B is not shown worse and the gap survives."},{"id":"I9","predictions_lines":"Amendment 2 items 1 and 2 (replaces 143-145)","reading":"Amendment 2 sets the decision floor per compared arm: each of A, B, C, D, E needs 12 scored ordinary_bounded runs (not HARNESS_FAILED, not NOT_RUN), and A, C, D, E also need the fallback rule: at least 2 scored runs in each fallback scenario and a fallback harness-failure share of at most 1/5. Any arm short gives INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE. The decision value is the first matching mapping rule, wrapped as ADOPT_CONDITIONALLY when H2 or H4 is SUPPORTED_FOR:fallback_reasoning and the base decision is not INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE."},{"id":"I10","predictions_lines":"163-170","reading":"Amendment 1: inputs under a results-2026-10-03 directory are pre-amendment. They may be scored alone, but every verdict is then INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE because they do not count toward the evidence floor. Mixing them with other files is refused."},{"id":"I11","predictions_lines":"126-130","reading":"Only Codex rows are scorable. Any other harness name is refused, because H1 to H4 name Codex model families."},{"id":"I12","predictions_lines":"103-105","reading":"H3 compares